OK.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.012
So that's a way of
thinking about some

00:07:59.012 --> 00:08:00.720
of the steps that
we'll talk about later,

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:03.050
in terms of how we're
going about doing marketing

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:03.810
analytics.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:07.290
Build a warehouse
of data, move--

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.390
create a visualization,
create some analytics

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:13.150
around that data, and
then activate on that.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.580
So moving on from there.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.040
Then, I think the
question, though, that--

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:20.600
when I'm talking to clients,
what they're really asking is,

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.042
why should marketing analytics
be a priority for my business?

00:08:24.042 --> 00:08:25.500
I'm going to propose
that there are

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:28.000
two things that are critically
important to you, here.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:31.660
One is the performance
of your business.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.470
And the second one is that
your customers are radically

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:35.320
changing.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.182
So let's look at
first one first--

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:38.390
performance of your business.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:41.580
So Forrester did
a report in 2016

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.700
where they looked across
businesses at performance

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.840
of the marketing function.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:49.240
And what they
found was companies

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:52.780
that have an integrated-- a
well-integrated marketing,

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.870
data, and tools
environment, really

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:57.370
are outperforming their peers.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.320
And they are outperforming
their peers roughly

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:02.200
by beating their budgets
each year by over 10%,

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.750
or their revenue
goals by over 10%.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.030
So that's a fairly
significant marker

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:09.040
for leading organizations.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:14.140
They also recognized that 35%
of the marketers they talked to

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:17.080
saw Return On Marketing
Investment, or ROMI,

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.690
as being one of the
most valuable metrics

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:23.665
that they had to secure
additional budgets

00:09:23.665 --> 00:09:26.630
for their marketing programs.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:30.370
However, almost all the folks
that Forrester talked to

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:33.400
found that most
of these marketers

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.520
didn't have a way of
actually measuring return

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:36.520
on marketing investment.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:39.220
And so clearly what
comes from that is really

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.080
a call for what we
were talking about

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.186
earlier, this idea of
an integrated data set,

00:09:43.186 --> 00:09:44.560
an integrated data
warehouse that

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:49.197
really spans across the
entire marketing function.

00:09:49.197 --> 00:09:50.530
Another way of looking at this--

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:55.480
McKinsey, 2017, asked
business leaders

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:58.550
across functions and
across industries,

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:02.500
how is big data and analytics
affecting your business?

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.370
You, perhaps, would
expect that the sectors

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.910
on the right-hand side of
this chart, high tech, energy,

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:13.030
and sectors like that are
impacted fairly substantially

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:15.500
by big data and analytics.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.500
What was really notable
to me, and, perhaps,

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.810
why I have this chart here,
is that sales and marketing

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:23.530
across industries was
noted by business leaders

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.860
as being heavily impacted
by big data and analytics.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.960
And so again, this
is another reason

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.840
why we see leading companies
now turning attention

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.850
to marketing data and
marketing analytics

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:38.630
because it is transformational
for their businesses.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:42.130
Second thing, then--
your customers.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:44.590
And the way that
I experience this

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.620
is probably the same
way that you do.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.016
I would ask you to just
reflect on the journey

00:10:50.016 --> 00:10:51.640
that you had-- the
physical journey you

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:58.190
had planning and getting to
Next over the past few days.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:02.260
How many humans did you
interact with in that process?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:06.160
I'll propose to you that number
is very, very small-- maybe

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.240
the person who checked
you in at the hotel.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:11.950
But most likely almost
all of your interactions

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.870
were done without
human intervention.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:18.160
And we're expecting and
research is showing us

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:22.740
that by 2020, 85% or more
of relationships between us,

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.510
as customers, and companies
is going to be done

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.430
without any human interaction.

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:29.170
And that puts a
tremendous burden on us

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:32.330
as marketers to really
understand our customers.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.230
And of course, we have the
same complementary issues

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:38.980
or opportunities being
presented to us around the move

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.660
from desktop to mobile.

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:42.899
We have customers' expectations.

00:11:42.899 --> 00:11:43.690
And I'm a customer.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:46.490
My expectations of the people I
work with are very, very high.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:48.760
I expect them to know me.

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:52.960
And so that change in the
way customers are behaving

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:59.230
is another driver behind this
need for integrated analytics

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.645
around marketing.

00:12:00.645 --> 00:12:02.770
And this is really because
our journeys have become

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:06.370
much more complex as customers.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.310
We're self-directed now.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:12.070
Back not that long ago,
marketers would essentially

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:15.760
be able to tell you how you
should experience their brand.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:19.380
That has completely been
flipped on its head, now.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.540
We, as consumers-- and I'm
putting myself in your place--

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:28.450
as a consumer, I'm deciding how
I experience your brand now.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.090
What order I ask
questions, what devices I

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:33.490
use, where I am
physically, whether I'm

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:37.390
using online or offline
contact with you--

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:40.150
all of that is completely
changing the way

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.160
that the customer
experience is occurring.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.870
Again, that drives
the need for us

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.350
to have a new way
of understanding

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:48.920
how that relationship works.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:51.440
What the customer
journey really is.

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:53.110
And just to compound
it, or maybe it's

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:57.640
all a part of the same
thing, we're more demanding.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:01.000
We expect marketers--
we expect the brands

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.970
that we work with
to understand us,

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.640
to be able to create this
seamless experience based

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:10.000
on intimate knowledge about
who we are and what we want.

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:18.550
And that means that we have to
really get to information that

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:25.120
is relevant and timely and
immediate for each interaction

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:27.710
that we have with a customer.

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:29.977
So our responses
have to be tailored.

00:13:29.977 --> 00:13:31.060
They have to be immediate.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.457
They have to meet our needs
for a short attention span.

00:13:33.457 --> 00:13:34.540
They have to be shareable.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.710
They have to be memorable.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.590
They have to be completely
relevant to your point of view

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:43.980
or your point in the journey
with that brand, at that time.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:50.352
So that takes us to,
how do we do this?

00:13:50.352 --> 00:13:52.810
So the second thing I wanted
to talk about today, as I said

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:58.435
at the outset was talk about a
framework on how we relate to

00:13:58.435 --> 00:14:00.730
or how we talk to
our customers and how

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:04.120
we're implementing these
types of solutions for them.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.670
So we have a fairly simple
marketing analytics framework.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:07.880
It consists of three pieces.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.840
And I'll go through
each of them in turn.

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:15.170
Building a comprehensive
marketing data warehouse.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:18.910
Second, developing
analytics and visualization.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:22.030
And third then driving on
top of that, machine learning

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:24.310
solutions.

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:28.970
First things first, let's
talk about the framework.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.055
Well, I'll put this in the
context of-- or excuse me.

00:14:32.055 --> 00:14:34.070
Not the framework, but
the data warehouse.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:36.160
Let's put this in the
context of a customer.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.450
Here's a customer.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:40.570
She's on the phone with
your contact center.

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:44.360
Well, for you to serve her
and to meet her expectations,

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.802
you need to know who she is.

00:14:45.802 --> 00:14:47.260
You need to know
about her journey.

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:50.350
You need to know what
her expectations are.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:53.020
What is she expecting to
get out of this conversation

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.470
that she's having with you?

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.380
Oh, and oh, by the
way, you probably

00:14:56.380 --> 00:15:00.040
also, in this interaction, want
to know what your objectives

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:00.850
are, as a marketer.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:01.930
What do you expect--

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:03.860
what do you want
her to experience?

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:07.840
And how do you want to influence
the journey that she's on?

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.400
And so to be able
to do that, we have

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.630
to have this kind of
comprehensive knowledge

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:15.850
of her experience so far.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.850
There are a lot of
data sources that we

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.420
need to bring to bear here.

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:23.080
And I, in my prior
life as a CMO,

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:27.370
I experienced the same
challenge that I've

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:30.790
talked about with many
marketers here this week.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:34.720
And that is that we have most
likely in our offices anywhere

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:37.630
between a dozen and
two or three dozen

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:40.660
different marketing
technology applications

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.850
that we use to do our jobs.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:46.090
And they are often
software as a service.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:49.480
They're tailored towards
specific parts of the marketing

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:50.560
process.

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:53.500
They have their own
individual data silos.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.330
Some of the very
large organizations,

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.760
like Salesforce--

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:01.300
some of them are custom,
maybe a warranty system

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:04.910
or a service system for
the automotive industry.

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:06.750
There are a lot of
third parties involved.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.208
Oh, and oh, yes,
of course, there's

00:16:08.208 --> 00:16:10.240
also a fair amount
of information

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.460
that we can get from
our partners at Google.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:16.930
So Google Ads and the
Google Marketing Platform--

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:20.380
we can bring all that data
in through the BigQuery data

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:21.340
transfer service.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:24.860
All of that becomes available
to us fairly quickly.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:28.420
But we also are writing
or using third parties

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:32.260
to integrate a number of--
all these other systems

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.200
into this one holistic
view of the customer.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.800
So we have to be able
to access all that data.

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:42.310
There is some quality
control we have to do.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.110
But we are getting
to the point where

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:47.860
we can look across
devices to get that one

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:49.510
view of the customer--
their journey,

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.456
both online and offline.

00:16:51.456 --> 00:16:53.080
And I think it's
important to note here

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:56.290
that our goal in
building this is

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:59.630
to look towards the ultimate
outcome for that customer.

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:01.470
So what happened at the end?

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:02.770
Did they buy?

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:03.780
Did they not buy?

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:06.579
Did they-- what is
our lifetime value,

00:17:06.579 --> 00:17:09.770
either present or expected,
for that customer?

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:12.849
So we're going beyond just, now,
did I acquire that customer?

00:17:12.849 --> 00:17:14.589
Did they click onto my ad?

00:17:14.589 --> 00:17:16.280
I want to go all
the way to, what

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:17.530
is the value of that customer?

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.060
And what's the value--

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:21.450
how did that customer
experience the journey?

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:25.480
And what do we learn from that?

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:29.080
So there's a lot of data that
needs to be brought together.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:32.200
We've been doing this for AAA.

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:36.820
They came to us a couple of
years ago, now, and said, gee,

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:37.630
we have a problem.

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:40.030
And our problem is that we
have all these customers

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.980
and we have all
these business lines,

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:45.010
but we can't tell
what this customer is

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.750
doing across business lines.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.650
So can you help us with this?

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:51.940
And yes, we put together what
we describe as a modern data

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:52.570
platform.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:55.360
It's essentially that
marketing data warehouse

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:57.370
that I talked about
earlier, bringing data

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.770
from across the enterprise,
from across their marketing

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:02.650
applications, and from all
of their internal functions

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:05.674
to create that one
view of the customer.

00:18:05.674 --> 00:18:07.840
They've been using that for
a number of applications

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:10.000
from a marketing point of view.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.634
They've been using it to
do better targeting around

00:18:12.634 --> 00:18:13.300
their marketing.

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.430
So they're communicating
more effectively

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:18.147
and more consistently
with their customers.

00:18:18.147 --> 00:18:20.230
And their customers are
hearing from them messages

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:22.360
that are much more relevant.

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:26.650
They're also able to deliver a
much more consistent customer

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:28.240
experience and customer service.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:31.420
So if you call for
roadside service now,

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.100
they know everything about you.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:36.220
They know more than just
your car needs serviced.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:40.750
They know whether you are
insured by them, whether you

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.030
are a travel customer.

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.530
This may not be critical to you
when you've got a flat tire,

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:47.540
but the point being that
they have this holistic view,

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:51.070
and they can use that to create
much more seamless interactions

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:54.800
between themselves
and their customers.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:59.870
So second piece-- the
analytics and visualization.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:02.600
And this is where
things get obviously

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:03.770
a little bit more custom.

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.920
If you're an automotive
manufacturer,

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:08.390
you're looking
for certain things

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:11.037
from the analytics for
your customer's journey,

00:19:11.037 --> 00:19:12.620
obviously, that
experience is somewhat

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:15.680
different from if you're
selling soap powder,

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:18.500
for example, laundry detergent.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:22.430
But we do have some
templates that we start

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.030
from in those conversations.

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:27.650
And these are all
driven around, again,

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.530
what the marketers needs are.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:34.520
"OnBrand Magazine" did a
survey at the beginning of 2018

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:40.400
and asked what brand marketers
priorities were for 2018.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.560
You'll notice that three of the
top four bars on this chart,

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.640
so vast majority of folks,
are concerned about something

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.270
about the customer experience.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:52.370
This, again, drives this
issue that we have to--

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.860
we really have to
understand what

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:58.920
the customer is experiencing and
how to improve that experience.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.830
And so the analytics
that we're building,

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:04.430
the visualizations that we're
building are really around

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:07.250
helping them understand
that customer experience--

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:09.140
how to acquire
customers effectively,

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:10.600
how to retain them--

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.310
so minimizing churn if you
have a long-term business,

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.960
long-term relationship--

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:19.010
and how to enhance that
customer experience.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.810
At Crate and Barrel
over the last--

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:24.410
I think this was maybe a
year and a half ago now.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.030
They came to us
with a problem that

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:28.730
was kind of reflective of this
analytics and visualization

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:35.660
problem, which was many of
their internal processes were

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.820
difficult. They
were very manual.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:40.710
They, again, were not able to
bring a visualization together

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:43.550
or bring analytics together that
were helpful to their marketing

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.050
team.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:46.986
And they weren't able to make
decisions in a timely way.

00:20:46.986 --> 00:20:48.860
So we developed a set
of dashboards for them.

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:50.510
We automated a lot
of the reporting.

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:54.650
And we've reduced all their
routine reporting by maybe 10x.

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:57.500
And we're delivering much
better, much improved

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.510
timed insight for them.

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:05.330
They turned this into money
by identifying a real mismatch

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.790
between the time that they
were sending paper catalogs

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:11.850
through the mail, which are very
expensive, to their customers.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:13.880
And there was a
regional distribution

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.250
or a regional demand issue
that they hadn't seen before.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:19.520
They were able to time
these campaigns differently

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:23.690
and both reduce their costs
and improve response times

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:26.180
by delivering the right
catalog to the right customers

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:29.060
in the right region
at the right time.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:32.510
The last piece
I'll talk about is

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:33.856
the machine learning solutions.

00:21:33.856 --> 00:21:36.230
And here, you can go in a
number of different directions.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:38.657
As you might expect, I
have a different chart

00:21:38.657 --> 00:21:41.240
which I use sometimes, which is
kind of a checkerboard of here

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:43.520
are about a dozen
different sample

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:45.050
machine learning solutions.

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:47.450
You saw a couple earlier
in the demonstration

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:50.950
where we're targeting, what are
the right keywords to select

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:55.360
and what is the right bid
level for a specific vehicle?

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:57.620
And how do we select
the right incentives

00:21:57.620 --> 00:22:01.140
to go onto vehicles that have
been on the lot a long time?

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:05.940
A couple of other
samples for you--

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:08.300
customer segmentation
based on this holistic view

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.920
becomes much more empowered.

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:12.390
We're talking, now,
about being able to--

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:16.820
if it's a segment based on
specific behaviors in close

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:22.230
to real time, if not
actual real time--

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:25.550
so we're able to really create
much more meaningful segments

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:27.950
being able to address
specific offers to segments

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:30.050
on a much more fine
tuned basis because

00:22:30.050 --> 00:22:33.374
of our more holistic view.

00:22:33.374 --> 00:22:34.790
The second thing
that we're doing,

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:39.110
which, again, has been difficult
for marketers to do in the past

00:22:39.110 --> 00:22:44.030
is to really understand
attribution, which is now

00:22:44.030 --> 00:22:47.150
that we're looking at a complete
data set, which spans all

00:22:47.150 --> 00:22:51.170
the way from your first contact
with a brand, all the way

00:22:51.170 --> 00:22:54.170
through purchase or
nonpurchase, we're

00:22:54.170 --> 00:22:57.650
able to use machine learning
techniques to understand

00:22:57.650 --> 00:23:00.390
the value of each
marketing channel.

00:23:00.390 --> 00:23:04.550
So that allows us
now to say that,

00:23:04.550 --> 00:23:07.910
in this particular context,
for this segment of customers,

00:23:07.910 --> 00:23:10.010
digital is more
valuable than email,

00:23:10.010 --> 00:23:13.870
or digital is more valuable
than search, or vice versa.

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:16.079
The impact of that is
pretty significant.

00:23:16.079 --> 00:23:17.870
We take that with our
customers all the way

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:22.770
through optimization and
into marketing mix modeling,

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:24.980
so you can now
reshape your budgets

00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:27.170
based on a complete
understanding of what

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:30.650
the actual sales impact
is of the investments

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:34.340
that you've made in each
individual customer's journey.

00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:36.500
Going back to our friend
on the phone earlier,

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:39.650
that means that we can
go to her and, knowing

00:23:39.650 --> 00:23:42.380
what we do know now
about her journey,

00:23:42.380 --> 00:23:45.440
we can take that
next best action.

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:49.680
We can target the offer
to her, in this case,

00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:52.310
through the contact center
script that she's using,

00:23:52.310 --> 00:23:57.880
or that she's being exposed
to to get her on her journey

00:23:57.880 --> 00:24:00.950
to a place where she
has the best customer

00:24:00.950 --> 00:24:04.700
experience that she can get from
you, while at the same time,

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:07.790
you're managing her
towards the outcomes that

00:24:07.790 --> 00:24:10.860
are most profitable for you.

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:17.630
So we activate a lot of
these machine learning models

00:24:17.630 --> 00:24:19.130
through these
different channels.

00:24:19.130 --> 00:24:23.750
And of course, this varies
customer by customer,

00:24:23.750 --> 00:24:26.270
or client by client,
that we're working with,

00:24:26.270 --> 00:24:28.745
but activation now
is really something.

00:24:28.745 --> 00:24:31.700
And machine learning driven
activation is something.

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:33.290
It is a reality.

00:24:33.290 --> 00:24:35.090
It really is allowing
us, at this point,

00:24:35.090 --> 00:24:38.720
to target individually
right product,

00:24:38.720 --> 00:24:43.160
right offer, right customer,
right time, right channel.

00:24:43.160 --> 00:24:45.620
I would love to stand
here and say that we

00:24:45.620 --> 00:24:47.720
can do all this overnight.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:50.420
Clearly, we can't.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:55.220
And the way that we approach
this with our customers

00:24:55.220 --> 00:24:59.660
is to think of this
in an agile way.

00:24:59.660 --> 00:25:02.990
We develop softwares in
other parts of our business

00:25:02.990 --> 00:25:04.640
for our clients.

00:25:04.640 --> 00:25:07.530
And we use agile as our
core methodology there.

00:25:07.530 --> 00:25:09.896
And while it may be a--

00:25:09.896 --> 00:25:11.270
while you may not
expect it, this

00:25:11.270 --> 00:25:15.650
translates directly into what
we're doing for marketers.

00:25:15.650 --> 00:25:17.750
It does because
we're essentially

00:25:17.750 --> 00:25:22.310
following an iterative process
in delivering solutions

00:25:22.310 --> 00:25:23.930
to them.

00:25:23.930 --> 00:25:27.470
We think about it in
these five phases.

00:25:27.470 --> 00:25:31.586
And we would tend to go around
the circle multiple times

00:25:31.586 --> 00:25:32.960
for an engagement.

00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:36.370
So first of all, collecting
and transforming data.

00:25:36.370 --> 00:25:37.770
So collecting, as
I said earlier,

00:25:37.770 --> 00:25:40.700
we have a whole host of
different source applications

00:25:40.700 --> 00:25:43.970
that we're drawing data
from, transforming that data,

00:25:43.970 --> 00:25:48.230
and making it available
in the data warehouse.

00:25:48.230 --> 00:25:50.600
Analyzing and
visualizing that data.

00:25:50.600 --> 00:25:52.730
So analysis is great,
but it's not useful

00:25:52.730 --> 00:25:55.261
unless you can actually see it
and have folks make decisions

00:25:55.261 --> 00:25:55.760
on it.

00:25:55.760 --> 00:25:57.500
So analyze and visualize.

00:25:57.500 --> 00:26:00.297
And then activate that
through the marketing channels

00:26:00.297 --> 00:26:01.130
that I said earlier.

00:26:01.130 --> 00:26:04.130
So actually connecting
back, generally through APIs

00:26:04.130 --> 00:26:07.270
to those delivery systems.

00:26:07.270 --> 00:26:10.700
So you're delivering
the right message

00:26:10.700 --> 00:26:13.730
to the right
customer, right time.

00:26:13.730 --> 00:26:16.550
We go through this
cycle multiple times.

00:26:16.550 --> 00:26:19.880
It's important that you not
get stuck at any one point.

00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:22.640
I encourage you, if you're
going down this path,

00:26:22.640 --> 00:26:25.130
to think about use cases first.

00:26:25.130 --> 00:26:28.040
What's the data that drives
the use case that drives value?

00:26:28.040 --> 00:26:29.450
Go around the cycle.

00:26:29.450 --> 00:26:31.310
Get some return on investment.

00:26:31.310 --> 00:26:36.009
Show leadership that this is
essentially paying for itself.

00:26:36.009 --> 00:26:37.550
That's going to
secure the investment

00:26:37.550 --> 00:26:39.805
to do the next iteration
and the one after that.

00:26:39.805 --> 00:26:41.180
And that's the
way that I've been

00:26:41.180 --> 00:26:42.730
doing this for quite some time.

00:26:42.730 --> 00:26:46.850
And we're able to move
forward with these projects

00:26:46.850 --> 00:26:49.670
pretty rapidly and at
the same time, show

00:26:49.670 --> 00:26:51.130
return to the business.

00:26:51.130 --> 00:26:55.280
And there's nothing like
showing a monetary return

00:26:55.280 --> 00:27:00.080
on this investment to secure
investment for the next cycle.

00:27:00.080 --> 00:27:01.360
So that's the journey.

00:27:01.360 --> 00:27:05.460
And I would encourage you to
think about it as a journey.

00:27:05.460 --> 00:27:11.510
So you can map those phases
to the Cloud Platform products

00:27:11.510 --> 00:27:13.440
that we're using.

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:16.775
As you would expect,
BigQuery is the home,

00:27:16.775 --> 00:27:18.400
and as I've described
earlier, BigQuery

00:27:18.400 --> 00:27:23.930
is the home for the data
warehouses that we build.

00:27:23.930 --> 00:27:29.820
We use other tools from the
GCP suite to ingest data,

00:27:29.820 --> 00:27:32.480
whether it's streaming
or batch from all

00:27:32.480 --> 00:27:35.840
these different applications.

00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:39.530
For analytics, we use Datalab.

00:27:39.530 --> 00:27:44.030
We use the Cloud ML
Engine to do analytics

00:27:44.030 --> 00:27:46.550
based on what's in BigQuery.

00:27:46.550 --> 00:27:49.250
Of course, many of
the ML capabilities

00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:51.241
are now merging into
BigQuery, so a lot of this

00:27:51.241 --> 00:27:53.240
is going to end up probably
in that one hexagon.

00:27:53.240 --> 00:27:57.350
But we've been using a number
of these tools in the past

00:27:57.350 --> 00:27:59.720
to get us to this point.

00:27:59.720 --> 00:28:02.210
For visualization,
Data Studio is

00:28:02.210 --> 00:28:03.570
ramping up faster and faster.

00:28:03.570 --> 00:28:05.870
We're getting a lot of
traction now and using

00:28:05.870 --> 00:28:07.860
Data Studio with our clients.

00:28:07.860 --> 00:28:09.200
We do use partner products.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:13.190
And I think my colleagues
on the Google side

00:28:13.190 --> 00:28:17.765
recognize that clients
have investments

00:28:17.765 --> 00:28:19.610
in Tableau and in Looker.

00:28:19.610 --> 00:28:22.100
And so as a services
organization,

00:28:22.100 --> 00:28:26.180
we certainly work with
those solutions, too,

00:28:26.180 --> 00:28:29.340
to deliver the visualizations
they're looking for.

00:28:29.340 --> 00:28:36.410
And then, in activation, this
is where we're publishing--

00:28:36.410 --> 00:28:39.740
we can publish solutions
from the machine learning

00:28:39.740 --> 00:28:41.992
that we're doing as APIs.

00:28:41.992 --> 00:28:44.520
And they can be
consumed that way.

00:28:44.520 --> 00:28:46.990
Some of the marketing
technologies that we work with

00:28:46.990 --> 00:28:50.090
are still batch oriented
and some of the data

00:28:50.090 --> 00:28:52.270
is not so volatile that
you need to have an API,

00:28:52.270 --> 00:28:56.590
so you can deliver
through batch, as well.

00:28:56.590 --> 00:28:58.330
And then that's
essentially the way

00:28:58.330 --> 00:29:02.090
we're delivering and activating
to each of these technologies.

00:29:02.090 --> 00:29:09.640
So that gives you a sense of the
scope of how we're delivering

00:29:09.640 --> 00:29:13.630
and how our customers are
integrating their marketing

00:29:13.630 --> 00:29:16.000
analytics or delivering
their marketing analytics,

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:19.240
using the Google Cloud Platform.

00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:24.670
So hopefully, that gives you an
idea of how we, as Maven Wave,

00:29:24.670 --> 00:29:27.070
are working with the
Google Cloud Platform

00:29:27.070 --> 00:29:31.360
to deliver against the goals
of marketing analytics.

00:29:31.360 --> 00:29:33.510
You know, as a
former CMO, I wish

00:29:33.510 --> 00:29:34.887
I had had this a few years ago.

00:29:34.887 --> 00:29:36.970
I think it is really game
changing for the clients

00:29:36.970 --> 00:29:38.284
that we're working with.

00:29:38.284 --> 00:29:39.700
And I'll just leave
you in summary

00:29:39.700 --> 00:29:42.580
with these three thoughts.

00:29:42.580 --> 00:29:46.420
First of all, really this
integrated marketing analytics

00:29:46.420 --> 00:29:48.760
is a marker, now, of
high performing marketing

00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:49.690
organizations.

00:29:49.690 --> 00:29:52.570
And the leading enterprises
that we're working with

00:29:52.570 --> 00:29:54.580
recognize this is game
changing for them.

00:29:54.580 --> 00:29:56.470
If you think back to
that McKinsey chart

00:29:56.470 --> 00:29:59.440
that I showed earlier,
analytics and big data

00:29:59.440 --> 00:30:01.780
are transformational
for sales and marketing

00:30:01.780 --> 00:30:03.400
across all industries.

00:30:03.400 --> 00:30:05.360
It's not a one size
fits all solution,

00:30:05.360 --> 00:30:07.660
but it's
transformational for all.

00:30:07.660 --> 00:30:12.280
And so this is really a
marker of the companies

00:30:12.280 --> 00:30:16.270
that are going to be
leading in their industries.

00:30:16.270 --> 00:30:18.980
A comprehensive
marketing data warehouse

00:30:18.980 --> 00:30:21.370
is essential foundation.

00:30:21.370 --> 00:30:23.030
It doesn't all get
built in one day,

00:30:23.030 --> 00:30:24.670
but it is really
the foundation, both

00:30:24.670 --> 00:30:26.830
for doing analytics
and visualization

00:30:26.830 --> 00:30:28.940
and then getting to
machine learning.

00:30:28.940 --> 00:30:30.732
So the machine learning
is going to deliver

00:30:30.732 --> 00:30:32.356
the insights and
actions that are going

00:30:32.356 --> 00:30:33.465
to delight your customers.

00:30:33.465 --> 00:30:36.160
And at the end of the day,
it's all about the customer

00:30:36.160 --> 00:30:39.400
experience and
delighting that customer.

00:30:39.400 --> 00:30:42.360
Last, and most importantly,
is this is a journey.

00:30:42.360 --> 00:30:45.620
This is not something that
is going to happen overnight.

00:30:45.620 --> 00:30:50.420
But if you start now, you will
be ahead of your competitors.

00:30:50.420 --> 00:30:53.500
Go back and look at
that five circle chart,

00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:56.380
and start with collecting
that essential data

00:30:56.380 --> 00:30:58.450
for that first use case.

00:30:58.450 --> 00:31:03.140
Deliver some value, and
you'll be ahead of the curve,

00:31:03.140 --> 00:31:07.390
I think, on your analytics,
your marketing environment

00:31:07.390 --> 00:31:09.710
versus those of
your competitors.

00:31:09.710 --> 00:31:13.360
So that's all I had to
